# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must never be committed.
#   cp .env.example .env

# The key for the live model, layer 3 of the demo architecture. It is read by the
# server process only and never reaches the browser.
#
# Leave it blank and everything still works: every question is answered from the
# hand reviewed cache in data/answers.json, and anything the cache does not cover
# gets the prepared refusal. That is the same path the demo takes in production
# once the monthly budget is spent, so running with no key is a real test of it.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Where novel questions go. gpt-5-nano is the cheapest current OpenAI text model at
# $0.05 per 1M input tokens and $0.40 per 1M output. gpt-5-mini and gpt-5 are also
# priced in server.mjs if you want to trade cost for quality.
DEMO_MODEL=gpt-5-nano

# HMAC key for the signed session token, control 16. Any long random string.
#   node -e "console.log(crypto.randomUUID())"
#
# Left blank, the server generates a fresh one at boot, which quietly invalidates
# every open session on restart. Fine locally, wrong for anything deployed.
DEMO_SECRET=

# ---- Cloudflare only, not used by server.mjs ------------------------------
# These are set on the Pages project, never in a file. Listed here so the full
# set is in one place.
#
#   DEMO_KV           KV namespace binding. Counters, budget and CV requests.
#   TURNSTILE_SECRET  Splits the budget into a verified and an unverified pool.
#   RESEND_API_KEY    Optional. Absent, CV requests are stored and not emailed.
#   CV_NOTIFY_TO      Optional. Where a CV request notification goes.
#   CV_NOTIFY_FROM    Optional. A verified sender on the domain.
